.TH MU2EDAQ-POWER-SEQUENCE.YAML 5 "2026-09-18" "mu2edaq-power-recovery 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
power-sequence.yaml \- phase 2 power-on stage order for the Mu2e DAQ
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I config/power-sequence.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
Defines the order in which the cluster is brought up, as data rather than code:
.BR mu2e-power-on (1)
is the engine that walks this file.
.PP
The order is operational, not arbitrary.
.I mu2e-mgr-01
exports
.I /home
and the shared areas, so every later node's NFS mounts fail if it is not up and
healthy first; the data loggers and DCS servers must be serving before the CFO
and the readout nodes have anywhere to write; the CFO distributes the clock and
control fabric the tracker, calorimeter, CRV and STM nodes synchronise to.
.SH STRUCTURE
.SS defaults
Values inherited by every stage that does not set its own:
.IR location ", " require ", " concurrency ", " power_on ", " boot_timeout ", " settle .
.I checks
is deliberately
.I not
inheritable: a stage with no
.I checks
key runs the profile of each node's own host class, which is rarely what a
whole-stage default would have meant.
.SS stages
An ordered list. Each stage runs only after the previous one reached its
.I require
state.
.TP
.I name
Short identifier, used in the report and by
.BR \-\-from / \-\-until
(and by
.IR run.from_stage / run.until_stage ,
which they override). Matching is exact and a name that matches nothing is
.I not
an error:
.B \-\-from
falls back to the first stage and
.B \-\-until
to the last, so a typo runs more of the sequence than intended, not less.
Check the stage list with
.B \-\-until
naming the last stage you want and no
.BR \-\-execute .
A stage with no
.I name
is reported as
.B unnamed
and cannot be selected.
.TP
.I title
Human label for the report tables.
.TP
.I nodes
Explicit hostnames and NodeRange mappings, in the same syntax as
.BR mu2edaq-topology.yaml (5).
.TP
.I location
Topology location the nodes belong to. Default
.IR mc2 .
.TP
.I checks
Check profile from
.BR mu2edaq-checks.yaml (5)
applied after power-on.
.TP
.I require
How much of the stage must pass before the next may start:
.RS
.TP
.B all
Every node. The default, and correct for anything the rest of the cluster
depends on.
.TP
.B majority
More than half. Used for the readout nodes, where one dead machine should not
hold up the rest \(em the report still lists every failure.
.TP
.B any
At least one. Used for the gateways: one working jump host is enough.
.RE
.IP
Any other value is treated as
.BR all .
A stage whose
.I nodes
resolve to nothing never meets its requirement, whatever is set here \(em an
empty stage is a topology mistake, not a pass.
.TP
.I concurrency
Maximum nodes worked on at once within the stage.
.TP
.I power_on
When false the stage verifies only and never issues a power command. The
gateway stage sets this, because power-cycling a jump host removes the path
every later stage depends on. It is belt and braces: those hosts are also in
.I protected
in
.BR mu2edaq-topology.yaml (5),
which refuses destructive verbs for them wherever the request comes from.
.IP
A node in the stage with no BMC in the topology is recorded as
.B no_bmc
rather than passed over, so "we could not power this one on" is visible on the
checklist.
.TP
.I boot_timeout
Seconds to wait for SSH to answer after
.BR "chassis power on" .
.TP
.I settle
Seconds to wait after SSH answers before running checks, so that late-starting
units \(em NFS automounts, network-online targets, DTC firmware load \(em are
not sampled mid-start. The wait is skipped entirely when nothing in the stage
actually had to be switched on.
.SH THE SHIPPED SEQUENCE
.TP
.B gateways
.IR mu2egateway01 ", " mu2egateway02 .
Verify only,
.IR require: any .
.TP
.B manager
.IR mu2e-mgr-01 .
The NFS and home server;
.IR require: all ,
concurrency 1.
.TP
.B dataloggers
.IR mu2e-dl-01 ", " mu2e-dl-02 .
.TP
.B dcs
.IR mu2e-dcs-01 ", " mu2e-dcs-02 .
Additionally verifies that the shared areas are mounted from
.I mu2e-mgr-01
specifically, not merely that something is mounted there.
.TP
.B cfo
.IR mu2e-cfo-01 ,
including its PCIe device and driver.
.TP
.B readout
.IR mu2e-crv-01 ", " "mu2e-trk-01..14" ", " "mu2e-calo-01..11" ", " mu2e-stm-01 ", " mu2e-stm-02 .
.IR require: majority ,
concurrency 8.
.SH EXAMPLES
Add a stage after the CFO:
.RS
.EX
\- name: extmon
  title: Extinction monitor
  checks: readout
  concurrency: 1
  nodes:
    \- mu2e-extmon-01.fnal.gov
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run only part of the sequence:
.RS
.EX
mu2e-power-on \-\-execute \-\-from manager \-\-until cfo
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2e-power-on (1),
.BR mu2edaq-topology.yaml (5),
.BR mu2edaq-checks.yaml (5)
.SH AUTHOR
A. Norman <anorman@fnal.gov>, Mu2e DAQ Operations.
